So Tokido winning Evo I think
the reaction was like jubilation at

00:11:07.760 --> 00:11:14.060
least that's what I was seeing.
Tokido is beloved mainstay of the FGC of

00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:17.060
Street Fighter specifically. I mean if
you talk to someone who loves fighting

00:11:17.060 --> 00:11:20.780
games and they don't love Tokido,
I would have some questions for that

00:11:20.780 --> 00:11:24.950
person. He had an incredible loser's
bracket run through Evo and he

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:29.420
came up against the most promising young
player of this year I think it would be

00:11:29.420 --> 00:11:35.420
difficult to dispute, Punk, in the Grand
Finals and Punk had so much hype so much

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:41.030
heat going into that. Tokido comes in with
a character that by some accounts is not

00:11:41.030 --> 00:11:45.560
quite an S tier or an A tier character
not quite up to par in the form of Akuma

00:11:45.560 --> 00:11:50.810
and some people, myself included, had some
doubts whether that character could

00:11:50.810 --> 00:11:54.740
carry Tokido to where he needed to be to
where his skill was as a player. He was

00:11:54.740 --> 00:11:58.790
in his element it was a legendary win. I
think the reaction was just was

00:11:58.790 --> 00:12:01.330
jubilation.

00:12:01.330 --> 00:12:04.900
Caster: Tokido is the evolution 2017 champion!

00:12:04.900 --> 00:12:07.540
Coming all the way from losers bracket. He's done it!

00:12:09.100 --> 00:12:13.420
Finally he's been chasing it for so long.

00:12:13.540 --> 00:12:18.940
Armada winning Evo I think was, obviously was a big deal for him you know and that it's he's he finally has

00:12:18.950 --> 00:12:22.250
that second Evo he can he can work
towards the three-peat he's tied with

00:12:22.250 --> 00:12:26.600
Mang0 for Evo wins and that kind of
kind of evens up that rivalry or really

00:12:26.600 --> 00:12:30.260
pushes it in favor of Armada. It was a
cap to an incredible season for Armada

00:12:30.260 --> 00:12:34.970
following you know his loss to Hungrybox
in 2016. That was sort of a very big

00:12:34.970 --> 00:12:41.570
emotional moment for Armada as he told me and I think that after that, that lit

00:12:41.570 --> 00:12:45.740
a fire under him to just win
everything and he did. He was the

00:12:45.740 --> 00:12:50.240
undisputed best in the world by the end
of 2016 and going into 201, Evo 2017,

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:56.500
that Armada's tournament.

00:12:57.000 --> 00:13:02.980
Finally this month we saw the first
seven Overwatch League team owners

00:13:02.990 --> 00:13:10.520
announced. Misfits, Immortals, NRG, 
Patriots owner Robert Kraft, New York

00:13:10.520 --> 00:13:15.260
Mets COO Jeff Wilpon, Chinese game
publisher

00:13:15.260 --> 00:13:23.360
NetEase and Korean-American esports org
KSV, took the first seven spots.

00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:28.339
August brought TI7 where Team Liquid won a hard-earned 3-0

00:13:28.339 --> 00:13:34.310
victory over Newbee to take home the
aegis.

00:13:44.390 --> 00:13:50.339
Also this month, Optic Gaming defeated
Team EnVy to take home the 2017 Call of

00:13:50.340 --> 00:13:57.240
Duty World Championship.

00:14:02.920 --> 00:14:08.040
Finally in August, we got a few more
Overwatch League teams in Cloud9 and

00:14:08.040 --> 00:14:14.940
the Kroenke family which owns the LA
Rams, the Denver Nuggets and Arsenal.

00:14:15.720 --> 00:14:20.679
Moving on to September, we saw the final
Overwatch League team owners announced.

00:14:20.679 --> 00:14:26.559
Optic Gaming, Team EnVy and Comcast
Spectacor, which owns the Philadelphia

00:14:26.560 --> 00:14:31.240
Flyers, bought in completing the 12 team
initial lineup.

00:14:31.420 --> 00:14:35.559
The kinds of organizations and investors who we've seen buy into the Overwatch League kind of fills

00:14:35.559 --> 00:14:40.449
me and I think some people, with a lot of
hope regarding the future of esports. We've

00:14:40.449 --> 00:14:44.679
seen a lot and I mean a lot of
traditional sports investors get into

00:14:44.679 --> 00:14:48.009
esports in last year across with League
of Legends and Overwatch. The Overwatch League has

00:14:48.009 --> 00:14:54.279
a few though kind of for my taste not
quite enough traditional esports endemic

00:14:54.279 --> 00:14:58.959
teams involved. It's got venture
capitalists investors and it's got sort

00:14:58.959 --> 00:15:03.160
of a wide array and diverse array of
investment in it, which is really

00:15:03.160 --> 00:15:06.669
interesting and exciting to see. I think with
League of Legends right now we're

00:15:06.669 --> 00:15:10.169
basically only seeing esports teams and
sports teams so seeing also that mix of

00:15:10.169 --> 00:15:14.889
VC money is really cool.

00:15:14.889 --> 00:15:19.509
Traditional sports helped to define the unique structure of the Overwatch League our

00:15:19.509 --> 00:15:23.799
goal is to create the world's premier
eSport League where teams and players

00:15:23.799 --> 00:15:28.869
can thrive for years to come and fans
are made for life.

00:15:28.869 --> 00:15:34.020
H2K gaming co-chair Richard Lippe
released a statement threatening to have

00:15:34.020 --> 00:15:42.580
H2K leave the EU LCS if significant
changes weren't made to the system for the 2018 season.

00:15:42.580 --> 00:15:47.619
The EU LCS is basically, to put it bluntly, in shambles. Viewership

00:15:47.619 --> 00:15:51.579
in EU is lower than it has been for a
long time and we've seen a lot of

00:15:51.579 --> 00:15:55.720
concerns about that over a pretty long
period of time, but also Riot just seems

00:15:55.720 --> 00:15:59.799
to be unsure about what they want to do
with Europe. I think, and we've spoken to

00:15:59.799 --> 00:16:03.879
a lot of European you know, coaches, team
owners and players and a lot of people

00:16:03.879 --> 00:16:08.259
feel like Riot is just experimenting
with the EU LCS. Europe has been through

00:16:08.259 --> 00:16:12.910
so many sort of
diverse attempts at making this region

00:16:12.910 --> 00:16:16.480
work. We went to best of two's for a
while and then probably the biggest

00:16:16.480 --> 00:16:21.910
example of Riot's inability to decide
what they want to do with Europe came in

00:16:21.910 --> 00:16:28.750
the reported alternative format for 2018
which was 24 teams spread out across

00:16:28.750 --> 00:16:32.720
many regions. Basically we would have a
series of national leagues and then one

00:16:32.720 --> 00:16:37.860
larger league to mirror the European
football space.

00:16:37.880 --> 00:16:44.400
in September the biggest cs:go story of the year broke. Immortals cs:go team showed up late to

00:16:44.400 --> 00:16:48.380
their Grand Finals game at Dreamhack
Montreal.

